        "photoSource": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Empire_State_Building_from_Rockefeller_Center_New_York_City_dllu_(cropped).jpg",
        "description": "Nat came to New York for the Recurse Center in the spring of 2015 and stayed, settling in Brooklyn. Over the next few years he worked at littleBits, Hillary for America, First Look Media and Google.\n\nMel and Nat met on the Hillary Clinton 2016 presidential campaign, where they both worked in the Brooklyn headquarters. Mel was on the Research team and Nat was on the Tech team. Mel has a deep love of dogs, and a dog named Winnie sat next to Nat at the office, so Mel came by to pet Winnie almost every day.\n\nTheir first date was a Thundercat show at the Brooklyn Bowl. Because the campaign was seven days a week, they saw each other every day, and by the end of the summer conventions they were deeply in love.\n\nAfter the campaign ended they both decided to stay in Brooklyn. By May of 2017 they were living together, along with Mel's cat Beasley, who took to Nat quite well.\n\nMel and Nat were married in Prospect Park on May 12th, 2018."
      },
